---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: "Gyeonggi-do decline-designated counties"
description: "The Gyeonggi-do and Incheon counties that qualify for the F-1-D visa's lower, non-capital income threshold despite sitting inside the capital area."
permalink: "/regions/gyeonggi-do/population-decline-counties/"
---
{# Not paginated like regions/region.njk — Gyeonggi-do is the only capital-tier region, so it's
   the only place a population-decline county can change the eligibility outcome (architecture.md
   §7). Redesign style: same wide .region-page shell + two-column headline as region.njk, with a
   tinted threshold-summary card in place of the rent recap. #}
{% set declineCounties = [] %}
{% set watchCounties = [] %}
{% for c in populationDeclineAreas %}
{% if c.category == "decline" %}{% set pushed = declineCounties.push(c) %}{% else %}{% set pushed = watchCounties.push(c) %}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{% macro tierCard(c) %}
{% set photo = countyHeroPhotos[c.countyNameEn] %}
{% set credit = countyHeroCredits.photos[photo] %}
<li class="tier-card">
  <figure class="tier-card__figure">
    {% if photo %}<img class="tier-card__img" src="/assets/img/hero/gyeonggi-do-population-decline/{{ photo }}" alt="{{ credit.titleEn }}" loading="lazy">{% endif %}
    {% if credit.titleEn %}
    <figcaption class="tier-card__spot">
      <span class="tier-card__spot-en">{{ credit.titleEn }}</span>
      {% if credit.titleKo %}<span class="tier-card__spot-ko" lang="ko">{{ credit.titleKo }}</span>{% endif %}
    </figcaption>
    {% endif %}
  </figure>
  <div class="tier-card__body">
    <p class="tier-card__name">{{ c.countyNameEn }} <span class="tier-card__ko" lang="ko">{{ c.countyNameKo }}</span></p>
    <p class="tier-card__metro">{{ c.metroEn }}</p>
  </div>
</li>
{% endmacro %}

<div class="content-page region-page county-page">

<nav class="region-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
  <a href="/#map">Regions</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
  <a href="/regions/gyeonggi-do/">Gyeonggi-do</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
  <span class="region-breadcrumb__here">Decline-designated counties</span>
</nav>

<header class="region-header region-header--split">
  <div class="region-header__main">
    <span class="region-header__rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <h1>Gyeonggi-do decline-designated counties</h1>
    <p class="county-page__ko" lang="ko">경기도 인구감소지역</p>
    <p class="region-header__intro">
      Gyeonggi-do is a capital-area region, so its F-1-D income threshold is the country's
      highest. Seven counties are the exception.
    </p>
    <p class="region-header__intro">
      They sit inside the capital area administratively, but the government lists them as
      population-decline or watch-list areas — so they are assessed at the lower, non-capital
      threshold. Everything else in Gyeonggi-do and Incheon uses the capital figure.
    </p>
  </div>

  <aside class="region-header__aside">
    <div class="threshold-card">
      <p class="threshold-card__lead">
        These seven counties are assessed at Korea's non-capital F-1-D income threshold — the
        same as Gangwon-do or Jeolla-do.
      </p>
      <dl class="threshold-card__table">
        <div>
          <dt>In these seven counties</dt>
          <dd>₩{{ visaRules.thresholdsByMultiplier["1"] / 1000000 }}M–{{ visaRules.thresholdsByMultiplier["1.5"] / 1000000 }}M</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Rest of Gyeonggi-do &amp; Incheon</dt>
          <dd>₩{{ visaRules.thresholdsByMultiplier["1.5"] / 1000000 }}M–{{ visaRules.thresholdsByMultiplier["2"] / 1000000 }}M</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>How many qualify</dt>
          <dd>{{ declineCounties.length }} designated · {{ watchCounties.length }} watch-list</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
      <p class="threshold-card__note">
        Non-capital vs capital rate — the exact figure depends on your age and whether family
        join you.
      </p>
      <p class="threshold-card__links">
        <a href="/visa-info/">Visa info →</a>
        <a href="/settling-in/">Settling in →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </aside>
</header>

<section class="region-section">
  <div class="source-note">
    <span class="source-note__head"><span class="source-note__tick" aria-hidden="true"></span>Source:</span>
    <div class="region-guides__item">
      <a class="region-guides__link" href="https://www.mois.go.kr/frt/sub/a06/b06/populationDecline/screen.do" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Population-decline area designation ↗</a>
      <span class="region-guides__meta">mois.go.kr · Designated every 5 years, due October 2026</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="region-section region-section--tiers">
  <h2>The seven, by tier</h2>
  <p class="region-section__sub">Formally designated first, then the watch-list.</p>

  <div class="tier-group">
    <p class="tier-label">
      <span class="tier-chip tier-chip--designated">Designated · {{ declineCounties.length }}</span>
      Formally listed as population-decline areas.
    </p>
    <ul class="tier-grid">
      {% for c in declineCounties %}{{ tierCard(c) }}{% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="tier-group">
    <p class="tier-label">
      <span class="tier-chip tier-chip--watch">Watch-list · {{ watchCounties.length }}</span>
      Monitored, not yet designated — status can change year to year.
    </p>
    <ul class="tier-grid">
      {% for c in watchCounties %}{{ tierCard(c) }}{% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>

  <p class="data-provenance">Source: © Korea Tourism Organization (한국관광공사).</p>
</section>

</div>
